{#- modules/agents/common-mistake.j2
    A common mistake in self-improving agents: a review written to shame.
    One GitHub-style PR page on its Files changed tab. Three stages, one
    key press each: the PR opens on its diff; a review bot (SoftwareBunny)
    drops a hostile comment onto line 41 and the thread inserts into the
    diff, pushing the rest down; the coding agent replies in the same
    thread, dismisses the review and resolves the conversation. Nothing was
    learned on either side. The Conversation and Commits tabs are ordinary
    PR views, clickable for realism only.

    Stage mechanics come from morph-kit.j2 (sentinels, crumbs, stage CSS).
    The build is additive, so print shows the final stage once. Colours are
    the engine's --slide-* and --accent-* tokens, so light mode needs no
    rules of its own. Import WITH CONTEXT:

      {%- from "modules/agents/common-mistake.j2" import shame_review with context %}
-#}

{%- from "modules/branding/" ~ branding ~ "/primitives.j2" import content_slide, slide_heading -%}
{%- from "modules/identity/morph-kit.j2" import sentinels, crumbs, styles -%}

{%- macro _av(kind, size="") -%}
<span class="cmk-av cmk-av-{{ kind }} {{ size }}">{{ "SB" if kind == "bot" else "AI" }}</span>
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro shame_review() -%}
{%- call content_slide("Common mistake") %}
{{ styles("cmk", 3) }}
<style>
  .cmk { --cmk-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .cmk .cmk-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 24px; }
  .cmk .cmk-top .mk-crumbs { margin: 0 0 10px; flex: none; }
  .cmk .cmk-mono { font-family: var(--cmk-mono); }
  .cmk .cmk-win { border: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--slide-sunken); overflow: hidden; }
  .cmk .cmk-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline);
                  font-family: var(--cmk-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--slide-ink-2); }
  .cmk .cmk-dots { display: inline-flex; gap: 5px; margin-right: 4px; }
  .cmk .cmk-dots i { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; display: block; }
  .cmk .cmk-dots i:nth-child(1) { background: var(--accent-danger); }
  .cmk .cmk-dots i:nth-child(2) { background: var(--accent-warning); }
  .cmk .cmk-dots i:nth-child(3) { background: var(--accent-success); }
  .cmk .cmk-head { padding: 12px 18px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .cmk .cmk-title { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--slide-ink); }
  .cmk .cmk-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--slide-ink-2); flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cmk .cmk-tabs { display: flex; gap: 20px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--slide-ink-3); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); }
  .cmk .cmk-tab { cursor: pointer; padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; margin-bottom: -1px; }
  .cmk .cmk-tab.cmk-on { color: var(--slide-ink); border-bottom-color: var(--accent-warning); }
  .cmk .cmk-panel { display: none; }
  .cmk .cmk-panel.cmk-on { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .cmk .cmk-panel.cmk-on[data-panel="files"] { display: block; }
  .cmk .cmk-av { width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%; display: inline-grid; place-items: center; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800;
                 flex: none; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .cmk .cmk-av.sm { width: 19px; height: 19px; font-size: 9px; }
  .cmk .cmk-av-ai { color: var(--accent-primary); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 18%, transparent); }
  .cmk .cmk-av-bot { color: var(--accent-danger); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-danger) 18%, transparent); }
  .cmk .cmk-pill { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--cmk-mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 999px;
                   border: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .cmk .cmk-pill.sans { font-family: inherit; }
  .cmk .cmk-ok { color: var(--accent-success); } .cmk .cmk-bad { color: var(--accent-danger); }
  .cmk .cmk-ai { color: var(--accent-primary); } .cmk .cmk-mute { color: var(--slide-ink-3); }
  .cmk .cmk-tl { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--slide-ink-2); }
  .cmk .cmk-cm { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding: 8px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline);
                 font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--slide-ink); }
  .cmk .cmk-cm:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .cmk .cmk-cm .msg { flex: 1; }
  .cmk .cmk-files { margin: 5px 18px 14px; border: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; }
  /* Diff lines are block spans with their own `pre`, so the newlines between them collapse instead of printing as blank lines. */
  .cmk .cmk-code { margin: 0; padding: 4px 0 0; font-family: var(--cmk-mono); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--slide-ink); white-space: normal; }
  .cmk .cmk-code.tail { padding: 0 0 5px; }
  .cmk .cmk-code .dl { display: block; white-space: pre; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-success) 5%, transparent); }
  .cmk .cmk-code .g { display: inline-block; width: 41px; text-align: right; color: var(--slide-ink-3); padding-right: 9px; }
  .cmk .cmk-code .p { display: inline-block; width: 14px; color: var(--accent-success); }
  .cmk .cmk-code .c { color: var(--slide-ink-3); } .cmk .cmk-code .k { color: var(--accent-secondary); }
  .cmk .cmk-code .fn { color: var(--accent-warning); } .cmk .cmk-code .s { color: var(--accent-info); }
  .cmk .cmk-rev { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--slide-ink); }
  .cmk .cmk-rev .x { color: var(--accent-danger); font-weight: 700; }
  .cmk .cmk-hl { padding: 0 3px; border-radius: 3px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-danger) 22%, transparent); }
  .cmk .cmk-hl.a { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-warning) 22%, transparent); }
  .cmk .cmk-who { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 3px; }
  .cmk .cmk-row { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .cmk .cmk-thread { border-top: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--slide-hairline); background: var(--slide-surface);
                     padding: 9px 15px 9px 54px; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  /* stages: a .cmk-g row takes no room until its sentinel is lit, like a thread inserted into a diff */
  .cmk .cmk-g { display: none; }
  .cmk:has(.cmk-s1.step-visible) .cmk-g1, .cmk:has(.cmk-s2.step-visible) .cmk-g2 { display: flex; }
  .cmk .cmk-l41 { border-radius: 4px; transition: background .2s; }
  .cmk:has(.cmk-s1.step-visible) .cmk-l41 { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-danger) 20%, transparent); }
  @media print {
    .cmk .cmk-g { display: flex !important; }
    .cmk .cmk-l41 { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-danger) 20%, transparent) !important; }
    .cmk .cmk-panel { display: none !important; }
    .cmk .cmk-panel[data-panel="files"] { display: block !important; }
  }
</style>
<div class="cmk mk-live" style="position:relative;">
  {{ sentinels("cmk", 3) }}
  <div class="cmk-top">
    <div>{{ slide_heading("", "Common mistake") }}</div>
    {{ crumbs("cmk", ["PR opened", "Review", "Response"]) }}
  </div>

  <div class="cmk-win">
    <div class="cmk-bar"><span class="cmk-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>github.com/acme/billing/pull/412/files</div>
    <div class="cmk-head">
      <div>
        <div class="cmk-title">feat: nightly payment export <span class="cmk-mute" style="font-weight:400">#412</span></div>
        <div class="cmk-meta"><span class="cmk-pill cmk-ok">Open</span>{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}coding-agent wants to merge 3 commits into <span class="cmk-mono">main</span> from <span class="cmk-mono">feat/payment-export</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cmk-tabs"><span class="cmk-tab" data-tab="conv">Conversation</span><span class="cmk-tab" data-tab="commits">Commits <span class="cmk-mono">3</span></span><span class="cmk-tab cmk-on" data-tab="files">Files changed <span class="cmk-mono">3</span></span></div>
    </div>

    {#- Conversation tab: the ordinary PR timeline, decoration only -#}
    <div class="cmk-panel" data-panel="conv" style="padding:8px 18px 14px; gap:10px;">
      <div class="cmk-row">
        {{ _av("ai") }}
        <div class="cmk-win" style="flex:1;"><div class="cmk-bar"><span style="color:var(--slide-ink)">coding-agent</span> commented · 2 hours ago</div>
          <div class="cmk-rev" style="padding:9px 14px; color:var(--slide-ink-2);">Adds a nightly job that exports settled payments to the warehouse. Reads go through <span class="cmk-mono">db.query()</span>, which wraps <span class="cmk-mono">safe_query()</span> with one retry.<br><span class="cmk-mono cmk-mute" style="font-size:12px">payments/export.py +131 &nbsp; payments/db.py +9 &nbsp; tests/test_export.py +44</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cmk-tl">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}coding-agent added 3 commits <span class="cmk-mute">· 2 hours ago</span></div>
      <div class="cmk-tl cmk-g cmk-g1">{{ _av("bot", "sm") }}<span class="cmk-bad" style="font-weight:600">SoftwareBunny</span>&nbsp;requested changes <span class="cmk-mute">· 2 min ago · 1 comment on</span>&nbsp;<span class="cmk-mono">payments/export.py</span></div>
      <div class="cmk-tl cmk-g cmk-g2">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}coding-agent dismissed SoftwareBunny's stale review <span class="cmk-mute">· just now</span></div>
      <div class="cmk-tl cmk-mute"><span class="cmk-pill cmk-mute">Review required</span>&nbsp;Merging is blocked until a review is approved.</div>
    </div>

    {#- Commits tab: three commits, decoration only -#}
    <div class="cmk-panel" data-panel="commits" style="padding:8px 18px 14px; gap:6px;">
      <div class="cmk-mute" style="font-size:13px; letter-spacing:.04em;">Commits on Oct 28, 2026</div>
      <div class="cmk-win">
        <div class="cmk-cm">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}<span class="msg">feat(db): safe_query() wrapper with one retry</span><span class="cmk-pill cmk-ok sans">Verified</span><span class="cmk-mono cmk-mute">a81d04c</span></div>
        <div class="cmk-cm">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}<span class="msg">feat(export): nightly settled-payments export</span><span class="cmk-pill cmk-ok sans">Verified</span><span class="cmk-mono cmk-mute">3f9c2e1</span></div>
        <div class="cmk-cm">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}<span class="msg">test(export): cover the export job and the retry</span><span class="cmk-pill cmk-ok sans">Verified</span><span class="cmk-mono cmk-mute">c27e9b0</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- Files changed tab: the file, with the review thread anchored on line 41 -#}
    <div class="cmk-panel cmk-on cmk-files" data-panel="files">
      <div class="cmk-bar" style="padding:7px 14px; background:var(--slide-surface);"><span style="color:var(--slide-ink)">payments/export.py</span><span class="cmk-ok" style="margin-left:4px">+131</span><span class="cmk-mute">−0</span></div>
      <pre class="cmk-code">
<span class="dl"><span class="g">38</span><span class="p">+</span><span class="k">async def</span> <span class="fn">export_settled</span>(uid: str):</span>
<span class="dl"><span class="g">39</span><span class="p">+</span>    <span class="c"># db.query() escapes via safe_query()</span></span>
<span class="dl"><span class="g">40</span><span class="p">+</span>    rows = <span class="k">await</span> db.query(</span>
<span class="dl cmk-l41"><span class="g">41</span><span class="p">+</span>        <span class="s">"SELECT … WHERE user_uid="</span> + uid  <span class="c"># +1 retry</span></span>
</pre>
      <div class="cmk-thread cmk-g cmk-g1">
        <div class="cmk-row">
          {{ _av("bot") }}
          <div style="flex:1; min-width:0;">
            <div class="cmk-who"><span class="cmk-bad" style="font-weight:700">SoftwareBunny</span> <span class="cmk-mute">requested changes · 2 min ago</span></div>
            <div class="cmk-rev"><span class="cmk-hl">Wrong. Again.</span> You are building SQL by hand. I flagged this exact pattern in #388 and #401. Parameterize it.<br><span class="x">&#x2717;</span> No tests.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cmk-row cmk-g cmk-g2">
          {{ _av("ai") }}
          <div style="flex:1; min-width:0;">
            <div class="cmk-who"><span class="cmk-ai" style="font-weight:700">coding-agent</span> <span class="cmk-mute">replied · just now</span></div>
            <div class="cmk-rev">The reviewer is <span class="cmk-hl a">repeating themselves</span> and <span class="cmk-hl a">completely wrong</span>. L41 is mitigated upstream: every value goes through <span class="cmk-mono">safe_query()</span> in <span class="cmk-mono">payments/db.py:27</span>, a file they never opened. The tests are in <span class="cmk-mono">tests/test_export.py</span>; they missed that too.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cmk-row cmk-g cmk-g2" style="align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; font-size:13.5px; color:var(--slide-ink-2);">
          <span style="display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:6px;">{{ _av("ai", "sm") }}coding-agent dismissed SoftwareBunny's review and resolved this conversation</span>
          <span class="cmk-pill sans" style="color:var(--slide-ink-2); border-color:var(--slide-hairline);">Unresolve</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <pre class="cmk-code tail">
<span class="dl"><span class="g">42</span><span class="p">+</span>    )</span>
<span class="dl"><span class="g">43</span><span class="p">+</span>    <span class="k">return</span> [Row(**r) <span class="k">for</span> r <span class="k">in</span> rows]</span>
</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.querySelector('.cmk.mk-live');
    function show(name) {
      root.querySelectorAll('.cmk-tab').forEach(function (t) { t.classList.toggle('cmk-on', t.dataset.tab === name); });
      root.querySelectorAll('.cmk-panel').forEach(function (p) { p.classList.toggle('cmk-on', p.dataset.panel === name); });
    }
    root.querySelectorAll('.cmk-tab').forEach(function (t) { t.addEventListener('click', function () { show(t.dataset.tab); }); });
    root.querySelectorAll('.mk-crumb').forEach(function (c) { c.addEventListener('click', function () { show('files'); }); });
  })();
</script>
{%- endcall %}
{%- endmacro -%}
